----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Wishing Spoiler
---------------

The most important use of Wishes is to make your character survive
longer.  First we will cover important attributes required to survive
longer. Followed by other good to have things and at the end some
other important items.


Magic Resistance
----------------
MR is only required after you have reached mid-game. It can become
painful from Dungeon level 7, when Polymorph traps and Level Teleport
Traps start to occur.  But these traps are not instant kills although
they could be very dangerous for your character.  The polymorph trap
can destroy your armour if it makes you something big or make you
naked and vulnerable if you turn out to be something small. Level
Teleport can send you on a different level in the middle of a host of
monsters without your pet. But still they are not instant kills. If
you are very unlucky a monster maybe generated with a wand of death.

There is no sure way to find MR randomly in the dungeon, except Cloak
of MR and Gray Dragon Scales or Scale Mail.

Wizards start of with Cloak of MR.

Ways to wish for MR.
a) blessed +3 Grey Dragon Scale Mail (unless you have magic
   resistance).
b) blessed greased fireproof +3 cloak of magic resistance (if you are
   a monk see above).
c) You could also wish for a MR giving quest artifact. But they all
   blast so you should have at least 40 hit points. The good thing
   about these quest artifacts is that they usually have extra
   benefits and these are safe items, in the end game. The Wizard and
   other Nasties don't try to steal them. Your own quest item is not
   safe. And you can use your armour or cloak slot for other things.

For neutrals (that want to use spells) The Eye of the Aethiopica is
the best option, except for Wizards who will get it anyway.

Other good artifacts are
- neutral The Platinum Yendorian Express Card: gives MR, telepathy,
  charging.
- neutral The Eyes of the Overworld: MR, Astral Vision, Enlightenment.
  It also protects against any light based attacks.
- lawful  The sceptre of might: MR + Conflict (very useful)
- lawful  The magic mirror of merlin: MR + Telepathy.
- unfortunately nothing for chaotics, they could use MagicBane though.

Some consider Enlightenment+Astral Vision to be greater than
Telepathy.  Charging is really mostly useful only for Tourist.

Also some consider Conflict as more important than Telepathy.

d) You could also wish for MagicBane and (remember to) wield it. It
   may blast non-neutrals so have atleast 24 hit points.


Poison Resistance
-----------------
PR is required as soon as possible as spiked pits and dart/arrow traps
are found very early. When large Orcs start to appear you better have
PR otherwise it is difficult to survive.

PR can be easily obtained by eating PR granting corpses (consult
monster manual). Before you obtain Unicorn Horn however it is only
advisable to eat the non-poisoness PR granting corpses.

Orcs, healer, barbarians, and tourists also start with it and Monks
get it at XL3.

Ways to wish for PR
a) blessed tin of green dragon meet.
b) blessed +3 Green Dragon Scale Mail.


Reflection
----------
In addition you must also have Reflection.  Reflection prevents ray
based attacks, like Wand of Death/Lightning/Fire/Cold etc. These ray
attacks do a lot of damage.  If you have low hitpoints it may as well
be an instant kill.  Also the monster will fire as many times it
can. So it is nearly a instakill, if you don't have MR.  It also
destroys a lot of stuff. It is important to get it as soon as
possible.

There is a 50% probability of finding Amulet of Reflection in Sokoban,
and another 50% probability of finding the shield of reflection in the
statue of Perseus in Medusa's Island.

Ways to wish for Reflection
a) blessed +3 Silver Dragon Scale Mail (unless you also have
   reflection, you may still want to get it because you may want to
   use the amulet slot, or you want to cast spells). But it is still
   better to do a reverse genocide of Silver Dragons, during the
   mid-level game.
b) blessed amulet of reflection (if monk see above).
c) Longbow of Diana - Only useful for non-ranger Chaotics. It must be
   wielded to get reflection and will blast at every wielding. Not
   really a good option.

Due to the difficulty of finding MR it is considered the highest
priority wish.  PR is not considered very important by most people
except the very seasoned players. If you do get a Wand of Wishing it
is important enough to spend a wish on it. Because you cannot let the
good fortune of finding the WoW go to waste.  Reflection comes in
between the two in priority, because it is very important in the early
game, and you may not find it eventually.


Armour
------
Armour is of prime importance, that is why you go on checking every
armour you find to use the best available. But wishing for the best
armour (a dragon scale mail) is not incompatible with wishing for the
three above attributes. So first wish should be spend on a DSM giving
an appropriate necessary attribute.  Once you have a DSM it is better
to wish for a magic marker (if you haven't found it already) before
going for different magic armour. The magic marker will allow you to
enchant your existing armour to high levels.

There are some other armour that are good to wish for.
1) Helm of Brilliance: Useful with Robe to allow even non-spellcasters
   to cast spells.
2) T-shirt: Normally easier to obtain from polymorphing stuff.


Athame
------
Magicbane or a rustproof athame can be very helpful in survival. It
allows one to engrave Elbereth semipermanently quite liberally.


Magic Marker
------------
This is the most wished for item in the game. It can increase the
effectiveness of your armours and weapons both. It should have a
higher priority than a good artifact weapon.

For wizards they are much more useful as they can write any spellbook
or scroll without knowning them with nearly 100% chance when luck is
maxed.


Bag of Holding
--------------
It is very important to not be burdened. This makes the bag of holding
a very important wish. It is very important for inventory management.
It is not impossible to live without one but it does get very
difficult and time consuming. It does get a higher priority than many
other things.


Wand of Polymorph
-----------------
Useful for obtaining any non-magical item without a wish. A very
useful item before entering gehennom as it can be used to fill the
holes in your inventory.


Ring of Free Action
-------------------
Although it can be obtained by polypiling, it is still a very
important item to have in the late game. As there are many ways that
can cause paralysis. It is a must have and may need to be wished if
not obtained by other means before entering Gehennom.


Weapon
------
A good weapon comes very low on wishing priorities as the best
strategy to play nethack is to not fight monsters directly but attack
them from far. So it is better to have a long range attack than a good
melee weapon. It is not recommended in the early game, as there are
far more important things to wish for. If a good artifact is required,
it may be possible to wish from the Castle wand.

The best weapons are
1) Grayswandir: Great all around weapon for anybody who can reach
   basic in this weapon. Difficult to get it unrestricted by
   sacrificing as the only other saber is Werebane. It doesn't destroy
   anything which makes it very good. It is not so bad even if
   restricted. The +5 to hit helps counter the restriction. And later
   with high luck restriction is not a problem.
2) Excalibur: Easy to get for Lawfuls at XL5. In addition to good
   attacks it also gives improved searching and Level drain
   resistance.
2) Frost brand: More effective in the hell, but destroys potions. Very
   easy to get unrestricted for lawfuls and neutrals as they get
     Excalibur or Vorpal blade on crowning. Not so easy for chaotics.
3) Fire brand: More effective in the planes, but destroyes potions,
   scrolls, spellbooks. Very easy to get unrestricted for neutrals and
   lawfuls.
4) Mjollnir: More effective in the hell, but destroys rings and
   wands. Easy to get for Valkyries by sacrificing. It is also a good
   long range weapon for Valkyrie if you have Gauntlets of Power, but
   beware it is a trap, as 1 times in hundred it will hit you, and
   when that happens you may loose your wands and rings.
5) MagicBane: Grants MR when wielded, absorbs curses, can engrave
   Elbereth, has useful other attacks. Works best at +7. Wizards get
   it easily by sacrificing.
6) Stormbringer: Level drains monsters and protects from level drain.
   Level drain also heals equal to half maxhp lost by the monster that
   was drained. The only trouble is that it attacks any peaceful/pets
   without any warning. It is useful only when not playing with pets,
   and playing carefully with peacefuls around.
7) Staff of Aesculapious: Only useful for Healers. A great weapon for
   the end game. Being a two handed weapon it is very dangerous if it
   gets cursed while wielded. So keep it blessed and check its blessed
   condition regularly. Can be invoked for curing sickness and
   sliming.
8) Spellbook of Magic Missiles: It is very useful for spellcasters. It
   does same damage at XL30 as Grayswandir, or twoweaponing two silver
   sabers against major demons. With the Eye of Aethiopica it becomes
   even more powerful. It does not destroy any object. It is also
   useful for non-spellcasters after they obtain a robe and/or helm of
   brilliance. Especially useful for Knights with Magic mirror of
   Merlin.
9) Gauntlets of Power: Very useful in the beginning game. Gives +6
   damage.
10) blessed +7 Daggers with expert skill.
11) blessed +7 poisoned arrows with expert skill. Except for LongBow
    of Diana there is no unlimited supply of arrows but it should be
    possible to obtain a few hundreds from arrow traps, gnomes and
    elves. At max luck the probability of disappearance is 0.5%. This
    means a stack of 200 should last 40K turns if each turn is spent
    firing one arrow. This is clearly enough for any normal game. It
    is also possible to wish for 20 silver arrows and use them through
    the whole of gehennom. You could go through gehennom faster with
    them.
12) blessed +7 poisoned darts with expert skill. Similar to arrows
    they are obtainable from kobolds and dart traps. With plenty of
    darts there is no need to carry heavy daggers.
13) Tooled horn only for Rogues, but it is better to polymorph other
    tools rather than wishing for it.

While wishing for Artifacts remember that they can be wished safely
only when there are less than two existing artifacts in the game.

Also understand that it is easier to obtain artifacts by sacrificing
corpses to your god. The first one will be given with a 1 in 10
chance, regardless of the number of artifacts in the game.

In addition Lawfuls get Excalibur (which is good enough for most
characters) very easily by dipping in fountains at XL5. Making it a
waste for Lawfuls to wish for artifacts.

For Chaotics it is quite easy to obtain Stormbringer as they will get
it when crowned. But it may not be so easy to wield it.

Grayswandir is so much better than the other wishable artifacts that
it is not much useful to wish for anything else.

Also Magic Missiles can be used by a lot of characters, especially
after you have obtained a robe and/or helm of brilliance.

My recommendations for different roles are
1) Archeologist - dwarvish mattock in the early to midgame and
   an artifact weapon in the late game.
2) Barbarian - starting weapon or a long sword in the early game
   Cleaver in the midgame and an artifact weapon in the late game.
3) Caveman - a Polearm in the early game and an artifact in the mid to
   late game.
4) Healer - Pets in the early game. Grayswandir or Staff of
   Aesculapius(Quest Artifact), and blessed +7 darts, in the mid to
   late game.
5) Knight - Excalibur in the early game and Excalibur and Magic
   Missiles in the late game.
6) Monk - martial arts in the early to mid game and Magic Missiles in
   the late game.
7) Priest - Club/polearm/morning star, whatever best weapon found in
   the early to midgame and an artifact weapon + magic missiles in the
   late game.
8) Ranger - Daggers in the early game. After maxing luck blessed +2
   arrows or darts upto midgame. blessed +7 darts, blessed +7 daggers,
   blessed +7 arrows in the late game. Till there are plentiful of
   dart there is no need to wield the bow so that you can wear a
   shield. And also there is no need to carry the heavy daggers.
9) Rogue - Daggers from beginning to end. There maybe a use for darts
   but the extra throw available for daggers is not available. It may
   still be useful to wish for an artifact melee weapon.
10) Samurai - Excalibur from the beginning to the end, possibly while
    two weaponing with the starting katana. Magic missiles may be used
    in the late game.
11) Tourist - Daggers in the early game blessed +2 darts in the mid
    game and blessed +7 daggers, blessed +7 darts in the late game,
    with magic missiles and an artifact weapon as a backup.
12) Valkyrie - Daggers and long sword in the early to mid game, and
    blessed +7 daggers and an artifact in the late game.
13) Wizard - Daggers in the early game, blessed +2 darts, daggers and
    magic missiles in the mid game, Magic Missiles and blessed +7
    darts for backup in the late game.

Gauntlets of power are very important for elves(as they cannot get
more than 18 strength) and also quite important for gnomes and orcs,
which cannot get more than 18/50. At 18 you get only 2 extra damage
bonus and at 18/50 you get only 3 extra damage bonus. If you are two
weaponing or using expert thrown daggers or darts, it matters quite a
bit 6-10 points of extra damage.

An early gauntlets of power can make a lot of difference for a
character, making it a good early wish. But it is not good for
spellcasters which don't have robes.


Wand of Wishing
---------------
Strategy for a wand of wishing is different than getting a random wish
from fountains (not really recommended), thrones, magic lamps, and
smoky potions.  A WoW is an item that can allow you to score your
first ascension, if used properly. It should not be wasted.

The first wish should always be 2 blessed scrolls of charging if
scroll of charging has not been identified. Otherwise it should be a
magic marker. This will allow you to use the full wand completely. It
is important to identify it if possible, but don't waste time in doing
that. There is a 1 in 127 chance that you will wrest out the last
charge when trying to zap an empty wand.

For the next two wishes you do not know whether they will be your last
wish, but you will know if it was the last wish. If it is the last
wish then wish using the above guidelines. Otherwise you know there
are more wishes left.

Next wish should be for SDSM so that you can cover up reflection. It
is also better than "oR because it leaves the amulet slot for
something else.

Wishing for Monk is very different. They get PR easily, Sokoban has
"oR. The only thing left is Magic Resistance, but they cannot use
CoMR, because that would replace the Robe, without which they cannot
spellcast very well.  So they must wait for HP 40 before wishing for
the EoA. For them the best wish very really on is Gauntlets of
power. Magic Markers are not that useful very early on because they
require blank scrolls. And you should only blank identified
scrolls. It is easy to blank scrolls in pools created by pickaxing a
fountain.

Next wish should be blessed tin of green dragon meat, if you don't
have PR.

After this you need one wish for MR, and for Monks one more maybe for
reflection. You also need to save one more wish for Magic Marker.

Now you must wish for the weapon. The best weapon depends on your
role, as noted above. But since this is an early wish a GoP should be
given a higher priority than an artifact weapon. Except for wizard and
healer everybody can use it. Even for these classes at very high
intelligence or wisdom levels it could be worn with very little
increase in failure rate. For Wizards Magic Missile is a special
spell, which will allow it to be cast. While for Healer most healing
spells are emergency (and these are the only ones he is not restricted
in). Later when they have obtained their maximum protection and killed
the minetown priest (via a buff pet) it can be worn more easily.

Beyond this point it becomes fuzzy as now it depends on what you need
most now. You may want to wish for enchant armour or weapon if you
cannot find them anywhere. A wizard may write them easily when
extremely lucky. Or you may wish for a bag of holding, or even a
blessed figurine of an Archon (but be prepared for it if turns out to
be hostile).

Now you should be strong enough to reach the castle and get the WoW
there to complete whatever you need there. But you should explore all
levels thoroughly before reaching there. So that you need to wish only
the things that you could not find anywhere. You may also wish for a
Wand of Polymorph to make things that you don't have.


Other useful items
------------------
Amulet of Life Saving: Very useful to prevent stupid deaths. Can be
polymorphed from other amulets.

Ring of Levitation or boots of levitation: Important for several
levels. Very useful in watery levels, on plane of air, and while
wielding a cockatrice corpse.

Speed Boots: An important item in the early to mid game. Is not
necessary for characters that can cast haste self even at a high
failure rate.

Jumping Boots: Useful for escape. It is still better than jump spell
as it does not need spell energy. It is better than speed boots in the
late game.

T-shirts: Can be polymorphed, easily as they are non-magical.


Miscellaneous
-------------
When wishing for an item always wish for a +2 or +3 item. Seasoned
players are divided on what is better. +3 gives more on average but +2
has a better chance of being useful immediately.

When wishing for stackable items you should wish for 2 items. 2 and 3
give similar items on average but 2 is better chance to be more useful
now. 20 Missiles (eg silver arrows) can be wished for at once. Also 7
candles are gauranteed.



